-- title:
--   Global quotient presentation of a Γ'-invariant affinoid-meromorphic function
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a domain $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring, with $\pi$ irreducible, $\mathcal O$ complete for the $\pi$-adic topology, residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ of cardinality $r$, and $(r)=(\pi)$; let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $v\det : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (multiplicatively written) satisfy: $v\det g=n$ exactly when $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$. Let $G$ be a group, $\sigma:G\to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, $\Gamma\le G$ containing an element mapping to a scalar matrix with $v\det=2$ and an element with $v\det=1$, and let $\Gamma'$ be the subgroup of those $x\in\Gamma$ with $v\det(\sigma x)$ even. Let $\rho:G\to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ be induced by $\sigma$, and assume the image $\rho(\Gamma')$ has finite stabiliser at every vertex of the lattice tree of $\mathcal O\subset K_0$ and meets every vertex orbit inside a fixed finite set of vertices. Let $C$ be a complete algebraically closed valued field over $K_0$ with value group $\Gamma_0$, let $\varpi$ be a pseudo-uniformizer of $K_0$ in $C$, and let $R$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra inside $C$ forming an adic frame for $(\pi,\varpi)$: $\pi$ irreducible, $R\to C$ injective with image exactly the valuation-$\le 1$ elements of $C$, $R$ complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, the elements of $K_0$ of valuation $\le 1$ exactly those of $\mathcal O$, the image of $K_0$ closed in $C$, and $\pi$ and $\varpi.\varpi$ having the same image in $C$. Assume further that for $x$ of valuation $<1$ and $y\neq 0$ some power $v(x)^n\le v(y)$, that every nonzero $\varepsilon\in\Gamma_0$ dominates $v(y)$ for some $y\neq 0$, that every point of the Drinfeld upper half plane $\Omega=C\setminus K_0$ lies in some affinoid $\Omega_n$ of the exhaustion attached to $\varpi$, and that the ring of functions on $\Omega$ holomorphic on every $\Omega_n$ is a domain. Let $F:\Omega\to C$ satisfy $F(w)=F(z)$ whenever $w=\rho(\gamma)z$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma'$ (Möbius action via `pmoebius`), and suppose for each $n$ there are $a,b$ holomorphic on $\Omega_n$ (uniform limits of uniformly bounded sequences of pole-free rational functions), with $b$ not identically zero and $b(z)F(z)=a(z)$ whenever $b(z)\neq 0$. Then there exist $\Phi,H$ holomorphic on every $\Omega_n$ with $H\neq 0$ such that for each $n$ there is a finite set $Z\subseteq\Omega_n$ with $H(z)F(z)=\Phi(z)$ for all $z\in\Omega_n\setminus Z$.
--
--   This is the globalisation step in the rigid-analytic half of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: a $\Gamma'$-invariant function that is meromorphic on each member of the affinoid exhaustion of Drinfeld's upper half plane is presented as a quotient $\Phi/H$ of two globally holomorphic functions. It feeds the construction of a ring homomorphism from the function field of the quotient curve into the field of $\Gamma'$-invariant meromorphic functions, [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_ringHom_functionField_invariantFieldOf_eval_of_chartwiseMeromorphic`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_ringHom_functionField_invariantFieldOf_eval_of_chartwiseMeromorphic).
